1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Researchers lose weeks to failed experiments. Worse, they sometimes publish conclusions drawn from experiments that succeeded technically and failed scientifically.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
This is LabGuard AI. It challenges the claim, protects the run, and only stops when the evidence can be trusted.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Here is the claim under test: Model B performs better than Model A. Reported on one seed. Model B trained ninety epochs against Model A's twenty-five. Both checkpoints picked on the test split.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Every one of those is a real property of the configuration. Nothing here is scripted.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
I start the verification. The Claim Analyst turns one sentence into eight measurable subclaims.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:41,000
The Scientific Skeptic reads the configuration and finds eleven loopholes. An eight percent positive rate makes accuracy nearly uninformative. The arms had unequal training budgets. Checkpoints were chosen on test.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:48,000
It also writes down the rival explanations it has to rule out, and which experiment would settle each one.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
The planner picks eight actions for twelve point six compute units, cheapest decisive checks first. Every action comes from a typed registry with validated parameters.

9
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The model can name an action. It can never issue a command. There is no path from model output to a shell, an eval, or a file write.

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,000
The five-seed retrain costs eight units against a six-unit threshold, so it stops for me. Nothing has run yet. Every job is holding at awaiting approval.

11
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
I approve. The jobs go out over Pub/Sub to a separate Cloud Run worker.

12
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:24,000
These curves are streaming from real training runs, epoch by epoch. RunMedic is watching each one.

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:32,000
First incident. Overfitting in the reported run: validation loss climbing away from its best while training loss keeps falling.

14
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:40,000
This one is a diagnostic replay of the reported run, so RunMedic records it rather than interrupting the measurement, and applies early stopping to the verification runs instead.

15
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Second incident. A submitted variant genuinely diverges to NaN. RunMedic caught it, scaled the learning rate down inside the bounds declared on the action, re-queued it, and it completed. Two attempts, fully audited.

16
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Third incident. The reported checkpoint fails its integrity check. LabGuard repaired and retried, got the identical failure signature, and stopped at three attempts rather than burning budget on a failure that was not changing.

17
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The Evidence Auditor then found the threshold subclaim still untested, planned a second round on its own, and ran it. That is the recursion: it keeps going until another experiment could not change a conclusion.

18
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Here is the verdict. Not sufficiently supported.

19
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Across five seeds under an equalised budget, the accuracy difference averages plus zero point zero zero six, with a ninety-five percent interval that contains zero.

20
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Macro F1 is negative. Model B loses on all five seeds. So does balanced accuracy.

21
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:42,000
The class-wise breakdown says why: the gain is entirely in the majority class, and minority recall drops from zero point four five to zero point three four. For a violence detector, that is the opposite of an improvement.

22
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Every score is a weighted pass rate over named checks, each showing its arithmetic. Data integrity is one hundred: there genuinely is no leakage, and the detector was proven on a positive control.

23
00:02:52,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Statistical stability is zero, and you can see exactly which three checks failed and the numbers behind them.

24
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Gemini writes the narrative. It is never allowed to produce a number. If its proposed verdict disagrees with the measured one, the measurement wins and the disagreement is written to the ledger.

25
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:18,000
The evidence ledger is the whole account: every agent, every action, the reason, the input, the result and the decision.

26
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:26,000
And the same engine runs on your own claim. A well-controlled ablation comes back fragile at confidence seventy-two. A fair but noisy comparison comes back not sufficiently supported at fifty.

27
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Seven agents on Gemini 3.5 Flash through Google ADK, sharing state in Firestore, with Pub/Sub and three Cloud Run services.

28
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Challenge the claim. Protect the run. Trust the result. LabGuard does not stop when the code runs. It stops when the evidence can be trusted.
